554
00:25:27,700 --> 00:25:28,467
Seriously, so cool.

555
00:25:28,467 --> 00:25:28,733
Yeah.

556
00:25:28,733 --> 00:25:31,067
Because she felt that all this needed

557
00:25:31,067 --> 00:25:32,367
was a straightforward answer.

558
00:25:32,367 --> 00:25:33,633
But after I finished talking,

559
00:25:34,133 --> 00:25:37,200
she ended up comforting me instead.

560
00:25:37,200 --> 00:25:38,433
That just didn't feel right.

561
00:25:39,067 --> 00:25:39,600
Not at all.

562
00:25:39,600 --> 00:25:41,167
It shouldn't be you comforting me.

563
00:25:42,433 --> 00:25:43,367
This whole thing

564
00:25:43,367 --> 00:25:44,467
was my fault from the start.

565
00:25:45,167 --> 00:25:46,300
In the end, my thought was

566
00:25:46,300 --> 00:25:48,433
I just wanted to

567
00:25:48,433 --> 00:25:49,800
give her back whatever time was left in the cabin

568
00:25:49,800 --> 00:25:52,100
as soon as possible.

569
00:25:52,800 --> 00:25:53,633
I get what you mean.

570
00:25:54,067 --> 00:25:55,533
That's why I said you feel really guilty.

571
00:25:55,533 --> 00:25:56,700
Part of it is

572
00:25:56,700 --> 00:25:58,733
that you're worried about wasting her time.

573
00:26:00,667 --> 00:26:02,500
So after you said everything, are you now

574
00:26:02,500 --> 00:26:04,167
feeling relieved, like a weight's been lifted off your shoulders?

575
00:26:23,333 --> 00:26:24,300
You guys heading out?

576
00:26:24,300 --> 00:26:25,167
Yeah, we’re going to play basketball.

577
00:26:25,167 --> 00:26:26,800
Oh, basketball? Then we’ll sit this one out.

578
00:26:26,800 --> 00:26:27,700
Go ahead.

579
00:26:27,700 --> 00:26:28,367
Okay.

580
00:26:29,033 --> 00:26:31,367
Bye.

581
00:26:32,167 --> 00:26:33,333
Bye.

582
00:26:34,167 --> 00:26:35,367
See you.

583
00:26:37,800 --> 00:26:39,600
If you want anything to eat, let us know and we’ll bring it back for you.

584
00:26:40,767 --> 00:26:42,667
If you want something, we can get takeout and bring it back.

585
00:26:42,667 --> 00:26:43,400
Okay, just get whatever you want.

586
00:26:43,400 --> 00:26:44,533
You guys decide.

587
00:27:34,567 --> 00:27:36,467
Wowo, you're still coughing.

588
00:27:41,067 --> 00:27:42,267
Are you still running a fever?

589
00:27:42,500 --> 00:27:43,600
Did you bring the thermometer with you?

590
00:27:43,600 --> 00:27:44,400
I didn't bring it.

591
00:27:44,400 --> 00:27:45,633
They should have one at the hospital, right?

592
00:27:49,167 --> 00:27:51,433
Should we go get a number now?

593
00:27:51,800 --> 00:27:53,767
Which department? Surgery?

594
00:27:53,767 --> 00:27:54,700
Which department?

595
00:27:55,333 --> 00:27:56,200
Internal medicine.

596
00:27:57,733 --> 00:27:58,733
Are you serious?

597
00:28:00,300 --> 00:28:01,567
Isn't this supposed to be surgery?

598
00:28:03,233 --> 00:28:03,533
I don't know.

599
00:28:03,533 --> 00:28:05,367
My mind is all over the place these days.

600
00:28:05,367 --> 00:28:06,633
I don't even know what I'm saying.

601
00:28:10,533 --> 00:28:11,233
Hey, driver.

602
00:28:12,567 --> 00:28:13,367
We're here, right?

603
00:28:14,233 --> 00:28:15,267
Okay.

604
00:28:17,133 --> 00:28:18,133
Put your coat on first.

605
00:28:18,367 --> 00:28:20,733
Brother Luo lent me this down jacket.

606
00:28:20,733 --> 00:28:22,267
He said I wasn't dressed warmly enough.

607
00:28:23,733 --> 00:28:24,567
It's so cold.

608
00:28:30,567 --> 00:28:32,033
Make sure your hat's on right.

609
00:28:33,000 --> 00:28:33,667
I haven't washed my hair.

610
00:28:33,667 --> 00:28:34,800
I feel a bit embarrassed wearing someone else's hat.

611
00:28:36,033 --> 00:28:36,733
It's okay.

612
00:28:37,333 --> 00:28:38,733
I'll wash it for them again.

613
00:28:40,600 --> 00:28:41,667
It's really cold today.

614
00:28:47,700 --> 00:28:48,700
How many days have you had a fever?

615
00:28:49,333 --> 00:28:51,300
Two days, I think. It started yesterday.

616
00:28:51,733 --> 00:28:53,200
There have been a lot of cases of influenza A lately.

617
00:28:53,200 --> 00:28:54,100
Let's take a routine blood sample.

618
00:28:54,100 --> 00:28:55,267
And let's test for COVID-19.

619
00:28:55,267 --> 00:28:56,233
And do nucleic acid tests for both influenza A and B.

620
00:28:56,233 --> 00:28:57,700
The results will be ready in about two to three hours.

621
00:28:57,700 --> 00:28:58,800
Come back for your follow-up once the results are ready.

622
00:28:58,800 --> 00:28:59,633
Okay, sure.

623
00:29:00,767 --> 00:29:01,800
Hang in there.

624
00:29:04,667 --> 00:29:05,600
Take a seat for now.

625
00:29:05,600 --> 00:29:06,433
Are you hungry?

626
00:29:06,433 --> 00:29:07,233
A little.

627
00:29:07,633 --> 00:29:09,633
Do you want some porridge or chicken noodle soup?

628
00:29:09,633 --> 00:29:11,233
Actually, I was thinking about that too.

629
00:29:11,233 --> 00:29:12,133
Okay, let's have that.

630
00:29:12,133 --> 00:29:12,733
Let's go with that.

631
00:29:13,433 --> 00:29:14,000
Let's go.

632
00:29:18,267 --> 00:29:19,133
You didn't bump into anything, did you?

633
00:29:19,133 --> 00:29:19,533
No.

634
00:29:20,333 --> 00:29:21,133
It's okay.

635
00:29:21,133 --> 00:29:23,600
You could use a guide dog right now.

636
00:29:25,067 --> 00:29:27,000
He says he's your guide dog.

637
00:29:27,433 --> 00:29:29,067
A bit clumsy.

638
00:29:29,067 --> 00:29:30,333
Watch out for the steps.

639
00:29:33,067 --> 00:29:34,100
It's so cold.

640
00:29:35,200 --> 00:29:36,533
It's so cold.

641
00:29:37,500 --> 00:29:39,167
I'll put two heat packs on you in a bit.

642
00:29:39,167 --> 00:29:40,067
Alright.

643
00:29:46,600 --> 00:29:49,167
Glass-Skin Crispy Pigeon

644
00:29:50,367 --> 00:29:52,067
You're not allowed to have this today.

645
00:29:52,067 --> 00:29:52,467
I won't eat it.

646
00:29:52,467 --> 00:29:53,633
Next time, I'll pack some for you to take home.

647
00:29:53,633 --> 00:29:55,067
I really won't.

648
00:29:55,067 --> 00:29:56,333
How about some congee?

649
00:29:57,200 --> 00:29:58,300
Anything's fine.

650
00:29:58,633 --> 00:30:00,300
I'm really cold right now.

651
00:30:00,300 --> 00:30:01,533
Can I have a heat pack?

652
00:30:01,533 --> 00:30:03,500
I didn't expect it to be so cold in the room.

653
00:30:03,500 --> 00:30:05,767
I'll put it on your back first.

654
00:30:05,767 --> 00:30:07,167
Then you can put one on the front yourself.

655
00:30:07,167 --> 00:30:08,800
If you need one on your back, I'll help you with it.

656
00:30:13,367 --> 00:30:14,567
This one doesn't seem to work very well.

657
00:30:14,567 --> 00:30:15,433
Let me get another one.

658
00:30:18,100 --> 00:30:20,733
But it shouldn't be too far from your clothes.

659
00:30:21,600 --> 00:30:23,333
So, maybe you could stick it on...

660
00:30:23,333 --> 00:30:24,167
Are you wearing something underneath?

661
00:30:24,167 --> 00:30:25,067
Yeah.

662
00:30:25,067 --> 00:30:25,533
Okay.

663
00:30:25,533 --> 00:30:26,633
Or how about here?

664
00:30:26,633 --> 00:30:27,633
This spot?

665
00:30:27,633 --> 00:30:28,467
Yeah.

666
00:30:29,333 --> 00:30:30,600
How about I put a few more on for you?

667
00:30:31,367 --> 00:30:32,100
No, that's enough.

668
00:30:32,100 --> 00:30:33,500
Just one in the front and one in the back is enough.

669
00:30:33,500 --> 00:30:35,433
No worries, I'll put another one on the back for you.

670
00:30:40,433 --> 00:30:42,733
Stick one over your spleen and stomach area.

671
00:30:43,433 --> 00:30:44,333
Put it on.

672
00:30:45,167 --> 00:30:46,567
Let me get you a cup of hot water.

673
00:30:48,000 --> 00:30:49,233
That's so thoughtful!

674
00:30:49,233 --> 00:30:49,600
That's right.

675
00:30:50,567 --> 00:30:52,533
Hi, could you pour me two cups of hot water, please?

676
00:30:58,333 --> 00:30:59,200
Here, this is

677
00:30:59,700 --> 00:31:00,567
a cup

678
00:31:00,567 --> 00:31:01,733
Maybe this room

679
00:31:01,733 --> 00:31:03,333
just isn't very warm to begin with

680
00:31:03,333 --> 00:31:04,333
Yeah

681
00:31:07,333 --> 00:31:08,333
Thanks

682
00:31:13,633 --> 00:31:14,800
Hey

683
00:31:14,800 --> 00:31:16,733
You’re so considerate

684
00:31:17,400 --> 00:31:19,300
You don’t really seem like the type

685
00:31:19,300 --> 00:31:21,333
