See, he came back to check on her right away.

1108
00:46:59,600 --> 00:47:01,067
He knows she's feeling really down.

1109
00:47:01,067 --> 00:47:02,033
Yeah.

1110
00:47:02,033 --> 00:47:02,667
Today,

1111
00:47:02,667 --> 00:47:05,100
she deliberately sat at the opposite corner from Lao Hu.

1112
00:47:11,633 --> 00:47:13,800
I did mention it a bit.

1113
00:47:13,800 --> 00:47:15,700
It seems like something's going on with them.

1114
00:47:16,300 --> 00:47:17,600
I could sense it.

1115
00:47:17,600 --> 00:47:19,233
I noticed everything.

1116
00:47:24,600 --> 00:47:26,767
I feel this is just the right moment

1117
00:47:26,767 --> 00:47:28,467
to give this gift to her.

1118
00:47:28,767 --> 00:47:30,767
All I hope is that she

1119
00:47:32,700 --> 00:47:34,267
can find herself again.

1120
00:47:34,367 --> 00:47:36,133
I just like that simple

1121
00:47:36,133 --> 00:47:37,667
and happy side of her.

1122
00:47:38,067 --> 00:47:39,500
I hope I can bring her

1123
00:47:39,500 --> 00:47:41,200
a bit of happiness.

1124
00:48:02,067 --> 00:48:03,133
Yonghao is actually pretty great.

1125
00:48:03,133 --> 00:48:04,267
It's just that one sentence.

1126
00:48:04,267 --> 00:48:05,467
Just finding yourself again is enough.

1127
00:48:05,467 --> 00:48:07,667
I just hope she can find herself again.

1128
00:48:08,067 --> 00:48:09,500
Just living simply and happily is enough.

1129
00:48:09,500 --> 00:48:11,300
He really acts like Xia Zhiguang.

1130
00:48:11,300 --> 00:48:12,067
Yeah.

1131
00:48:12,567 --> 00:48:13,800
Just now, in that last part,

1132
00:48:13,800 --> 00:48:17,533
we could see Xiao Hou looking after Wo Wo.

1133
00:48:17,533 --> 00:48:19,067
Including taking her to the hospital,

1134
00:48:19,067 --> 00:48:20,133
rushing back and forth,

1135
00:48:20,133 --> 00:48:22,200
and being so attentive and caring once they got home.

1136
00:48:22,200 --> 00:48:24,067
Honestly, this really got to me.

1137
00:48:24,067 --> 00:48:26,067
If he's still like this ten years from now, that would be amazing.

1138
00:48:26,467 --> 00:48:27,033
That's it.

1139
00:48:27,033 --> 00:48:27,533
Yeah.

1140
00:48:27,533 --> 00:48:28,000
Exactly.

1141
00:48:28,000 --> 00:48:29,567
Because in the early stages of a relationship,

1142
00:48:29,567 --> 00:48:31,433
especially during the courting phase,

1143
00:48:31,433 --> 00:48:32,700
it's totally normal.

1144
00:48:32,700 --> 00:48:34,167
No matter if it's the guy or the girl,

1145
00:48:34,167 --> 00:48:35,800
if one of you gets sick,

1146
00:48:35,800 --> 00:48:36,433
and you love them,

1147
00:48:36,433 --> 00:48:39,133
you should really take good care of them.

1148
00:48:39,333 --> 00:48:40,000
Right.

1149
00:48:40,333 --> 00:48:41,300
I have a really strong

1150
00:48:41,300 --> 00:48:42,733
and very personal feeling

1151
00:48:42,733 --> 00:48:44,233
that I just want to share with you all

1152
00:48:44,433 --> 00:48:48,233
Back in the early days, Hou Chengjie always gave me the impression

1153
00:48:48,233 --> 00:48:51,200
that whatever he said was always exactly right

1154
00:48:51,200 --> 00:48:52,233
always spot on

1155
00:48:52,233 --> 00:48:53,400
Like, were we thinking the same thing?

1156
00:48:53,400 --> 00:48:54,000
Right?

1157
00:48:54,000 --> 00:48:56,267
Yeah, at the time I just thought, wow, he's really good at this

1158
00:48:56,267 --> 00:48:56,633
It was like he

1159
00:48:56,633 --> 00:48:58,333
always had the perfect answer ready to go

1160
00:48:58,333 --> 00:48:59,700
He talked a lot

1161
00:48:59,700 --> 00:49:00,800
and was really articulate

1162
00:49:00,800 --> 00:49:01,667
So back then

1163
00:49:01,667 --> 00:49:02,733
the way he went after Wo Wo

1164
00:49:02,733 --> 00:49:04,233
just felt kind of unreal to me

1165
00:49:04,500 --> 00:49:05,700
Me too

1166
00:49:05,700 --> 00:49:07,267
Yeah, same here. He just seemed a little too perfect, you know? It didn't feel real

1167
00:49:07,267 --> 00:49:08,000
Yeah

1168
00:49:08,000 --> 00:49:08,567
Yeah

1169
00:49:08,567 --> 00:49:09,633
Sometimes I feel like

1170
00:49:09,633 --> 00:49:10,467
if he were a bit more awkward

1171
00:49:10,467 --> 00:49:12,800
or made some little mistakes

1172
00:49:12,800 --> 00:49:15,067
it would feel more genuine

1173
00:49:15,067 --> 00:49:16,533
And just now, in that scene

1174
00:49:16,533 --> 00:49:17,100
with the two of them

1175
00:49:17,100 --> 00:49:18,533
since Wo Wo was sick

1176
00:49:18,533 --> 00:49:20,200
and you could see she wasn't wearing any makeup or had her hair done

1177
00:49:20,200 --> 00:49:21,800
her acne scars and everything were just out in the open

1178
00:49:22,367 --> 00:49:23,567
I didn't say much more

1179
00:49:23,567 --> 00:49:24,533
but instead showed it through my actions

1180
00:49:24,533 --> 00:49:26,200
when I did certain things

1181
00:49:26,200 --> 00:49:28,400
Anyway, I felt that earlier

1182
00:49:28,400 --> 00:49:30,467
Xiao Hou seemed more real to me

1183
00:49:30,467 --> 00:49:31,500
Right

1184
00:49:31,500 --> 00:49:33,433
Actually, I liked what you just said

1185
00:49:33,433 --> 00:49:35,767
about that sense of change, the before and after

1186
00:49:35,767 --> 00:49:37,500
There are two things about Hou Chengjie that stood out to me

1187
00:49:37,500 --> 00:49:40,133
First, when he gave her medicine, he would say, "I've washed my hands."

1188
00:49:40,133 --> 00:49:41,300
He would say, "I've washed my hands."

1189
00:49:41,800 --> 00:49:43,133
And the second detail

1190
00:49:43,467 --> 00:49:44,500
that really got to me is

1191
00:49:44,500 --> 00:49:46,600
that I'm actually really afraid of getting sick

1192
00:49:46,600 --> 00:49:48,033
When he came back

1193
00:49:48,033 --> 00:49:50,333
Wo Wo asked him, "How did it go? What were the results?"

1194
00:49:50,333 --> 00:49:51,200
Hou Chengjie just said

1195
00:49:51,200 --> 00:49:52,467
"It's fine,"

1196
00:49:52,467 --> 00:49:53,467
"It's nothing."

1197
00:49:53,467 --> 00:49:55,133
That showed a lot of sensitivity

1198
00:49:55,133 --> 00:49:56,100
He cared about me

1199
00:49:56,100 --> 00:49:57,167
and didn't want to make it sound serious

1200
00:49:57,167 --> 00:49:58,067
and scare me

1201
00:49:58,367 --> 00:49:59,267
In that moment, I felt

1202
00:49:59,267 --> 00:50:01,033
that detail really touched me

1203
00:50:01,033 --> 00:50:02,000
It made me feel

1204
00:50:02,000 --> 00:50:02,733
I realized

1205
00:50:02,733 --> 00:50:04,067
how much I really like him

1206
00:50:05,100 --> 00:50:06,567
Honestly, I just feel like

1207
00:50:06,567 --> 00:50:08,267
his previous behavior of being anxious and insecure

1208
00:50:08,267 --> 00:50:09,100
and the way he made us feel

1209
00:50:09,100 --> 00:50:11,100
that he puts a lot of pressure on others

1210
00:50:11,100 --> 00:50:13,533
is actually just who he really is.

1211
00:50:13,533 --> 00:50:14,100
Yeah.

1212
00:50:14,100 --> 00:50:15,400
If he really was

1213
00:50:15,400 --> 00:50:16,667
as perfect as everyone imagines,

1214
00:50:16,667 --> 00:50:18,400
he shouldn't be so anxious and insecure.

1215
00:50:18,400 --> 00:50:19,300
He might just

1216
00:50:19,300 --> 00:50:20,700
say, "Okay, I respect you,"

1217
00:50:20,700 --> 00:50:21,433
and calmly talk things through with you.

1218
00:50:21,433 --> 00:50:22,667
He'd patiently explain everything.

1219
00:50:22,667 --> 00:50:24,000
It's only because he really likes her

1220
00:50:24,000 --> 00:50:25,100
that he gets so anxious and insecure.

1221
00:50:25,100 --> 00:50:26,333
That's why, in front of the camera,

1222
00:50:26,333 --> 00:50:27,167
he shows that side of himself

1223
00:50:27,167 --> 00:50:27,800
and makes everyone feel

1224
00:50:27,800 --> 00:50:29,067
the pressure he's under.

1225
00:50:29,400 --> 00:50:30,700
It's just that he likes her so much.

1226
00:50:30,700 --> 00:50:31,500
Yeah.

1227
00:50:31,767 --> 00:50:32,433
I think

1228
00:50:32,433 --> 00:50:35,800
when two people interact, the changing dynamics

1229
00:50:35,800 --> 00:50:37,700
can really bring out different sides in both of them.

1230
00:50:38,267 --> 00:50:40,333
I used to always complain.

1231
00:50:40,333 --> 00:50:42,433
I used to say that my wife was too strict with me.

1232
00:50:42,433 --> 00:50:43,633
She was always signing me up for tutoring classes.

1233
00:50:43,633 --> 00:50:44,667
It made me unhappy.

1234
00:50:44,667 --> 00:50:46,300
But when I got sick,

1235
00:50:46,300 --> 00:50:47,400
she treated my illness the same way.

1236
00:50:47,400 --> 00:50:49,400
She'd say about my illness,

1237
00:50:49,400 --> 00:50:50,367
"It's time to take your medicine."

1238
00:50:50,367 --> 00:50:51,267
"You have to take your medicine."

1239
00:50:51,267 --> 00:50:52,733
In the same tone,

1240
00:50:52,733 --> 00:50:53,800
and with the same approach

1241
00:50:53,800 --> 00:50:55,233
as when she signed me up for tutoring classes.

1242
00:50:55,233 --> 00:50:56,367
She's the same person.

1243
00:50:56,367 --> 00:50:58,167
But in different situations,

1244
00:50:58,167 --> 00:51:00,067
I have different feelings.

1245
00:51:00,067 --> 00:51:01,200
There's a good side to it.

1246
00:51:01,200 --> 00:51:02,000
I think

1247
00:51:02,000 --> 00:51:04,533
when I experienced her care while I was sick,

1248
00:51:04,533 --> 00:51:06,167
that care in that situation

1249
00:51:06,300 --> 00:51:07,667
but I also have to accept

1250
00:51:07,667 --> 00:51:09,600
her strictness with me in everyday life.

1251
00:51:09,600 --> 00:51:10,167
Yeah.

1252
00:51:10,167 --> 00:51:11,800
I think it's the same for Wo Wo.

1253
00:51:11,800 --> 00:51:13,333
Maybe you should also think about

1254
00:51:13,333 --> 00:51:16,300
whether, when you accept the good side of someone,

1255
00:51:16,600 --> 00:51:18,500
you should also accept their other side.

1256
00:51:18,500 --> 00:51:19,700
Sometimes, being too sensitive

1257
00:51:19,700 --> 00:51:20,300
can put a lot of pressure on you.

1258
00:51:20,300 --> 00:51:21,500
Yes.

1259
00:51:21,500 --> 00:51:23,167
That's a choice you have to make.

1260
00:51:23,167 --> 00:51:24,433
And I think there's something beautiful about that,

1261
00:51:24,433 --> 00:51:25,333
in my opinion.

1262
00:51:25,333 --> 00:51:26,800
Maybe it's something that takes both people

1263
00:51:26,800 --> 00:51:29,100
time to gradually accept about each other.

1264
00:51:30,000 --> 00:51:31,667
You put that really well.

1265
00:51:31,667 --> 00:51:33,800
Right.

1266
00:51:33,800 --> 00:51:35,533
Have you ever experienced something like that?

1267
00:51:36,167 --> 00:51:37,533
For example, times when you felt really weak,

1268
00:51:37,533 --> 00:51:38,600
like when you were sick.

1269
00:51:38,600 --> 00:51:40,100
I think everyone has probably gone through that at some point.

1270
00:51:41,200 --> 00:51:42,433
When I had surgery myself,

1271
00:51:42,433 --> 00:51:44,067
because it was during

1272
00:51:44,067 --> 00:51:44,667
a really unusual time.

1273
00:51:44,667 --> 00:51:45,467
Yeah, it was a really unusual time.

1274
00:51:45,467 --> 00:51:45,667
Yeah.

1275
00:51:45,667 --> 00:51:47,133
So when I had the surgery,

1276
00:51:47,500 --> 00:51:49,200
it was actually the first time in my life I’d ever had general anesthesia.

1277
00:51:49,700 --> 00:51:51,733
Getting around was really difficult at the time.

1278
00:51:51,733 --> 00:51:53,233
My family was in Hefei.

1279
00:51:53,233 --> 00:51:54,067
And I was in Beijing.

1280
00:51:54,067 --> 00:51:55,367
So I went to the hospital alone,

1281
00:51:55,367 --> 00:51:56,300
checked in by myself,

1282
00:51:56,300 --> 00:51:58,033
did all the pre-op tests on my own,

1283
00:51:58,033 --> 00:51:59,400
and then had the surgery under general anesthesia—all by myself.

1284
00:52:00,200 --> 00:52:01,400
Next time, call me, okay?

1285
00:52:02,033 --> 00:52:03,200
Sure, sis.

1286
00:52:03,200 --> 00:52:05,333
But deep down, you still kind of wish

1287
00:52:05,333 --> 00:52:07,033
someone could have been there at that moment

1288
00:52:07,033 --> 00:52:07,733
to look after you, right?

1289
00:52:07,733 --> 00:52:08,433
I’m not sure.

1290
00:52:08,433 --> 00:52:09,433
It’s just my personality—

1291
00:52:09,433 --> 00:52:10,633
I’m the type

1292
00:52:10,633 --> 00:52:12,333
who likes to try doing everything on my own.

1293
00:52:12,333 --> 00:52:15,467
So when I was under anesthesia,

1294
00:52:15,467 --> 00:52:17,467
there wasn’t a single friend or anyone else there.

1295
00:52:17,467 --> 00:52:18,633
I did feel a bit down at that moment.

1296
00:52:18,633 --> 00:52:20,300
But then I thought,

1297
00:52:20,633 --> 00:52:21,467
wow, I’m actually pretty awesome.

1298
00:52:21,467 --> 00:52:22,367
Yeah.

1299
00:52:22,367 --> 00:52:23,167
It’s kind of cool.

1300
00:52:23,467 --> 00:52:25,167
Yeah, I went through the whole thing by myself.

1301
00:52:26,067 --> 00:52:27,200
Pretty brave, actually.

1302
00:52:27,500 --> 00:52:28,600
What about you, Tangtang? Have you ever done something like that?

1303
00:52:31,000 --> 00:52:31,300
I think

1304
00:52:31,300 --> 00:52:32,733
after being together for so many years,

1305
00:52:32,733 --> 00:52:36,200
we've definitely looked out for each other at times.

1306
00:52:37,133 --> 00:52:40,200
I think that, up to now, the two of us

1307
00:52:40,200 --> 00:52:43,200
have been through some pretty rough moments

1308
00:52:43,467 --> 00:52:45,067
and we've both seen each other at our worst.

1309
00:52:46,067 --> 00:52:48,133
For example, I think that up to now,

1310
00:52:48,133 --> 00:52:49,367
the lowest point for me,

1311
00:52:49,367 --> 00:52:51,567
was during my confinement period after giving birth.

1312
00:52:51,567 --> 00:52:54,300
That whole time was extremely difficult and painful,

1313
00:52:54,300 --> 00:52:55,400
and I was really at my most vulnerable.

1314
00:52:55,400 --> 00:52:56,433
He saw all of this

1315
00:52:56,433 --> 00:52:59,467
and was there with me the whole time.

1316
00:52:59,467 --> 00:53:03,200
He also went through some rough patches himself.

1317
00:53:03,200 --> 00:53:05,400
I kept applying medicine for him

1318
00:53:05,400 --> 00:53:06,400
and stayed by his side.

1319
00:53:06,667 --> 00:53:08,367
So you two really support each other, don’t you?

1320
00:53:08,367 --> 00:53:08,800
Yes.

1321
00:53:08,800 --> 00:53:10,500
So I was just wondering,

1322
00:53:10,500 --> 00:53:12,100
ten or twenty years from now,

1323
00:53:12,100 --> 00:53:13,233
will it still be like this?

1324
00:53:13,233 --> 00:53:15,033
I think that's really important.

1325
00:53:15,667 --> 00:53:18,600
Actually, you notice that Wo Wo is also

1326
00:53:18,600 --> 00:53:20,667
in a rather vulnerable state.

1327
00:53:20,667 --> 00:53:21,767
Someone who’s sick

1328
00:53:21,767 --> 00:53:23,300
and maybe not feeling very optimistic.

1329
00:53:24,133 --> 00:53:25,000
So beautiful,

1330
00:53:25,000 --> 00:53:25,767
so radiant—that's the version of myself I showed

1331
00:53:25,767 --> 00:53:28,667
in front of Xiao Hou.

1332
00:53:28,667 --> 00:53:29,700
But when two people are together,

1333
00:53:29,700 --> 00:53:30,500
as they spend time with each other,

1334
00:53:30,500 --> 00:53:32,300
real things inevitably happen between them.

1335
00:53:32,300 --> 00:53:33,733
These experiences gradually allow your true self

1336
00:53:33,733 --> 00:53:35,733
to emerge, little by little.

1337
00:53:35,733 --> 00:53:37,300
And that's what makes you special to me,

1338
00:53:37,300 --> 00:53:39,067
or me special to you.

1339
00:53:39,067 --> 00:53:41,033
Because I've seen a side of you that no one else has.

1340
00:53:41,033 --> 00:53:41,500
Yes,

1341
00:53:41,500 --> 00:53:42,500
that side.

1342
00:53:42,500 --> 00:53:43,600
Exactly.

1343
00:53:44,433 --> 00:53:44,800
Let's go.

1344
00:53:44,800 --> 00:53:46,400
Tensions are running high in the cabin as well.

1345
00:53:46,400 --> 00:53:48,033
Let's keep watching their date.

1346
00:53:48,033 --> 00:53:48,767
Okay.

1347
00:53:54,567 --> 00:53:56,433
I love you

1348
00:53:56,433 --> 00:54:01,300
Not just because you're beautiful

1349
00:54:01,300 --> 00:54:02,267
President Su

1350
00:54:02,267 --> 00:54:04,333
I can see hope now

1351
00:54:04,333 --> 00:54:05,133
I'm even starting to hum a little song

1352
00:54:05,133 --> 00:54:10,433
Every glance from you touches my heart

1353
00:54:10,800 --> 00:54:11,800
Go grab the takeout

1354
00:54:18,067 --> 00:54:18,467
It's not cold.

1355
00:54:18,467 --> 00:54:19,067
It's fine.

1356
00:54:19,067 --> 00:54:19,800
Not particularly cold.

1357
00:54:20,667 --> 00:54:23,567
She's holding a wowo tou—a steamed corn bun—in her hands.

1358
00:54:23,567 --> 00:54:24,600
She seems a bit better today.

1359
00:54:26,033 --> 00:54:26,767
Yeah, she does seem better today.

1360
00:54:28,767 --> 00:54:29,333
Liang Tian...

1361
00:54:29,333 --> 00:54:30,167
She really does look better.

1362
00:54:32,100 --> 00:54:34,333
It just makes me really uncomfortable to see Liang Tian like this.

1363
00:54:37,033 --> 00:54:37,533
Not as upset?

1364
00:54:37,533 --> 00:54:38,167
Not like yesterday.

1365
00:54:38,167 --> 00:54:38,600
Right.

1366
00:54:40,500 --> 00:54:41,600
A couple of days ago,

1367
00:54:41,600 --> 00:54:42,800
I saw her

1368
00:54:42,800 --> 00:54:44,700
She and Lao Hu seemed a bit off.

1369
00:54:45,167 --> 00:54:46,533
You really notice the details.

1370
00:54:46,533 --> 00:54:48,067
Everyone noticed it too.

1371
00:54:48,600 --> 00:54:50,300
That was the day of the letter.

1372
00:54:50,300 --> 00:54:52,600
And then the misunderstanding just kept getting worse.

1373
00:54:53,000 --> 00:54:53,533
What happened?

1374
00:54:53,533 --> 00:54:55,000
I don't know either.

1375
00:54:57,233 --> 00:54:59,267
I thought they'd be doing well.

1376
00:54:59,267 --> 00:55:00,567
It's only been a few days, though.

1377
00:55:01,533 --> 00:55:04,067
Even an honest judge can't settle family matters, so it's best not to get involved.

1378
00:55:04,067 --> 00:55:05,433
I think when Lao Hu wants to talk,

1379
00:55:05,433 --> 00:55:06,533
for example, he'll let you know,

1380
00:55:06,533 --> 00:55:07,433
or something like that.

1381
00:55:08,000 --> 00:55:09,067
Or, you know?

1382
00:55:09,067 --> 00:55:10,667
Because I don't want to feel like

1383
00:55:10,667 --> 00:55:12,167
I'm taking advantage of the situation.

1384
00:55:14,000 --> 00:55:15,067
I get what you mean.

1385
00:55:16,133 --> 00:55:18,000
Yeah, I've always just been myself.

1386
00:55:18,000 --> 00:55:20,500
But now, from that point of view, it feels like...

1387
00:55:21,100 --> 00:55:22,333
So, are you still going to go after it?

1388
00:55:24,133 --> 00:55:24,533
Of course.

1389
00:55:24,533 --> 00:55:25,400
You will?

1390
00:55:25,400 --> 00:55:26,600
Yeah, I've always just done my own thing.

1391
00:55:26,600 --> 00:55:27,467
Just doing my own thing.

1392
00:55:27,733 --> 00:55:28,667
I'll keep at it.

1393
00:55:28,667 --> 00:55:31,100
Yeah, if there are still chances to go out

1394
00:55:31,100 --> 00:55:31,667
or choices to make,

1395
00:55:31,667 --> 00:55:32,500
