1396
00:55:32,667 --> 00:55:33,400
Got it.

1397
00:55:33,800 --> 00:55:35,000
That's pretty upfront of you.

1398
00:55:35,000 --> 00:55:36,500
Yeah, Yonghao's a really good guy.

1399
00:55:52,067 --> 00:55:53,167
Let me just put my shoes down.

1400
00:55:54,033 --> 00:55:54,400
Sure.

1401
00:56:03,267 --> 00:56:04,300
Have you been okay these past couple of days?

1402
00:56:05,067 --> 00:56:06,000
Have you been okay these past two days?

1403
00:56:06,000 --> 00:56:07,033
Not so great.

1404
00:56:07,733 --> 00:56:08,633
I know.

1405
00:56:08,633 --> 00:56:09,600
But I...

1406
00:56:10,433 --> 00:56:10,733
It'll be fine.

1407
00:56:10,733 --> 00:56:12,200
I'm actually much stronger than I thought I was.

1408
00:56:12,200 --> 00:56:13,133
A lot stronger, really.

1409
00:56:13,133 --> 00:56:15,600
I think I'm doing pretty well.

1410
00:56:16,367 --> 00:56:19,800
But I shouldn't force myself to act tough.

1411
00:56:20,633 --> 00:56:22,800
It's okay to have some emotions sometimes.

1412
00:56:23,500 --> 00:56:25,300
But I don't really see the need to get emotional.

1413
00:56:25,300 --> 00:56:26,700
It is what it is.

1414
00:56:26,700 --> 00:56:28,100
That's just how it is.

1415
00:56:29,300 --> 00:56:30,267
What else can I do?

1416
00:56:31,200 --> 00:56:32,533
I'm just a little puzzled.

1417
00:56:32,533 --> 00:56:33,400
It's just...

1418
00:56:33,700 --> 00:56:36,800
It's the kind of confusion I just can't figure out on my own.

1419
00:56:36,800 --> 00:56:37,433
And then...

1420
00:56:37,800 --> 00:56:40,000
But I don't think it's something that can be clearly explained.

1421
00:56:41,567 --> 00:56:42,433
I get it.

1422
00:56:43,300 --> 00:56:44,433
You probably understand, right?

1423
00:56:44,800 --> 00:56:45,500
Or maybe you don't.

1424
00:56:45,500 --> 00:56:46,500
Actually, you don't really get it.

1425
00:56:46,500 --> 00:56:47,367
I'm finished eating.

1426
00:56:47,667 --> 00:56:48,600
Maybe I should understand, right?

1427
00:56:51,200 --> 00:56:52,100
I don't understand you.

1428
00:56:52,433 --> 00:56:53,200
You don't understand me.

1429
00:56:53,200 --> 00:56:54,133
I don't understand you.

1430
00:56:54,133 --> 00:56:55,533
But I...

1431
00:56:57,533 --> 00:56:58,633
I don't dare to make predictions that far ahead either.

1432
00:56:58,633 --> 00:57:01,500
But I understand about 70-80% of what he's thinking (Hu Yunting).

1433
00:57:03,000 --> 00:57:04,067
You're talking about that situation.

1434
00:57:04,500 --> 00:57:05,700
Some things are just the way they are.

1435
00:57:05,700 --> 00:57:08,200
Let me tell a dark joke.

1436
00:57:08,533 --> 00:57:10,067
It's kind of like,

1437
00:57:10,300 --> 00:57:11,333
For example,

1438
00:57:12,433 --> 00:57:14,667
For example, if I get this kind of outcome with you,

1439
00:57:14,667 --> 00:57:15,333
It's the same for him.

1440
00:57:15,333 --> 00:57:18,067
I would also think, "That's just how it is."

1441
00:57:18,767 --> 00:57:19,333
Yeah, that's it.

1442
00:57:19,333 --> 00:57:20,100
That's just how he is.

1443
00:57:20,100 --> 00:57:21,000
That's just the way things are.

1444
00:57:21,000 --> 00:57:21,467
That's just the way it goes.

1445
00:57:21,467 --> 00:57:22,233
Yeah, that's right.

1446
00:57:22,233 --> 00:57:22,733
But I just...

1447
00:57:23,467 --> 00:57:24,233
I have my doubts, you know?

1448
00:57:24,233 --> 00:57:25,100
But I think this doubt...

1449
00:57:25,100 --> 00:57:26,533
there's really no point in questioning it further.

1450
00:57:26,533 --> 00:57:27,533
It's just that for me,

1451
00:57:27,533 --> 00:57:29,300
it causes a lot of inner turmoil.

1452
00:57:29,767 --> 00:57:30,767
It's pointless.

1453
00:57:31,267 --> 00:57:32,367
I know what you mean.

1454
00:57:32,667 --> 00:57:33,800
But if this stuff

1455
00:57:33,800 --> 00:57:35,433
really makes you unhappy,

1456
00:57:37,300 --> 00:57:40,167
Yonghao is taking his time looking up and matching information right now.

1457
00:57:40,167 --> 00:57:41,567
He's working on the questions now.

1458
00:57:41,567 --> 00:57:42,600
He'll definitely get it done.

1459
00:57:43,267 --> 00:57:44,400
I'm just about finished.

1460
00:57:44,400 --> 00:57:45,333
I might've still felt it yesterday.

1461
00:57:45,333 --> 00:57:46,433
But I'm feeling much better today.

1462
00:57:46,433 --> 00:57:48,267
Yeah, you'll definitely figure it out in the end.

1463
00:57:48,533 --> 00:57:50,567
But I think we can just have a chat.

1464
00:57:50,567 --> 00:57:51,333
Sure, let's chat.

1465
00:57:51,333 --> 00:57:52,367
Let's eat first.

1466
00:57:52,633 --> 00:57:53,800
Let me soak this for a bit.

1467
00:57:53,800 --> 00:57:54,700
Just set it aside for now.

1468
00:57:54,700 --> 00:57:55,667
Go ahead and eat a bit first.

1469
00:57:55,667 --> 00:57:56,733
It's okay.

1470
00:57:58,733 --> 00:58:00,000
What can you do?

1471
00:58:00,800 --> 00:58:01,667
Whatever.

1472
00:58:04,467 --> 00:58:05,533
For instance, take relationships.

1473
00:58:05,533 --> 00:58:06,633
I was talking to Xiaxia the other day,

1474
00:58:06,633 --> 00:58:07,700
I told her that when it comes to relationships,

1475
00:58:07,700 --> 00:58:09,367
it's marriage that can end in tragedy,

1476
00:58:09,367 --> 00:58:11,267
but love itself never does.

1477
00:58:11,733 --> 00:58:12,800
For example,

1478
00:58:15,800 --> 00:58:18,100
Let's talk about how you see life.

1479
00:58:18,100 --> 00:58:19,167
When you think about life,

1480
00:58:19,167 --> 00:58:20,533
everyone's life

1481
00:58:20,533 --> 00:58:21,733
ultimately ends the same way:

1482
00:58:21,733 --> 00:58:22,567
with death.

1483
00:58:23,433 --> 00:58:24,167
When we talk about death,

1484
00:58:24,167 --> 00:58:25,267
some people feel sad,

1485
00:58:25,267 --> 00:58:26,200
others get sentimental,

1486
00:58:26,767 --> 00:58:27,600
and see it as a tragedy.

1487
00:58:27,600 --> 00:58:30,367
But if your life is rich and full,

1488
00:58:30,367 --> 00:58:32,300
then your death isn't a tragedy.

1489
00:58:32,300 --> 00:58:33,700
The same goes for love.

1490
00:58:35,333 --> 00:58:38,500
Is autumn really just the tragedy of spring?

1491
00:58:39,233 --> 00:58:41,467
If the seeds you plant in spring bloom into flowers,

1492
00:58:41,467 --> 00:58:43,267
but don't bear fruit in autumn,

1493
00:58:43,267 --> 00:58:45,367
does that make autumn a tragedy?

1494
00:58:50,233 --> 00:58:51,100
Not necessarily.

1495
00:58:51,200 --> 00:58:54,300
You can't dismiss the flower that blossomed in spring

1496
00:58:54,300 --> 00:58:56,167
just because there was no fruit in autumn.

1497
00:58:56,167 --> 00:58:56,767
Exactly.

1498
00:58:57,800 --> 00:58:59,667
So, there's no such thing as tragedy in love.

1499
00:58:59,667 --> 00:59:01,467
Even those so-called tragic love stories people talk about—

1500
00:59:01,467 --> 00:59:03,033
the tragedies in legends and all that,

1501
00:59:03,033 --> 00:59:05,133
I don't think those relationships were really tragedies either.

1502
00:59:05,267 --> 00:59:07,567
That ending was simply autumn arriving.

1503
00:59:07,567 --> 00:59:08,333
Yeah.

1504
00:59:10,600 --> 00:59:11,667
So clear-headed.

1505
00:59:11,667 --> 00:59:13,633
Just look at that maturity.

1506
00:59:23,700 --> 00:59:25,400
Shi Tiesheng, My Days at the Temple of Earth

1507
00:59:25,400 --> 00:59:27,133
That was in autumn.

1508
00:59:34,233 --> 00:59:35,500
Thank you

1509
00:59:39,000 --> 00:59:40,300
