1591
01:01:56,800 --> 01:01:58,500
Time to conquer the world.

1592
01:01:59,267 --> 01:02:00,433
A perfect day.

1593
01:02:03,533 --> 01:02:04,700
I'll ride shotgun.

1594
01:02:04,700 --> 01:02:05,533
Sit down.

1595
01:02:05,533 --> 01:02:07,633
Come sit up front with me.

1596
01:02:19,700 --> 01:02:22,733
Okay, we're off, friends!

1597
01:02:27,033 --> 01:02:29,600
It really feels like we're going on an outing.

1598
01:02:29,600 --> 01:02:31,167
I'm so excited!

1599
01:02:31,700 --> 01:02:33,167
The weather is so nice today.

1600
01:02:33,167 --> 01:02:34,467
The sun is out.

1601
01:02:39,300 --> 01:02:40,533
It feels so nice.

1602
01:02:40,533 --> 01:02:41,167
But why

1603
01:02:41,167 --> 01:02:42,600
is there still a moon up there?

1604
01:02:43,567 --> 01:02:45,067
The moon's out way too early.

1605
01:02:45,067 --> 01:02:46,233
The moon.

1606
01:02:46,233 --> 01:02:48,333
Did the moon even set, or not?

1607
01:02:48,333 --> 01:02:49,367
Let's stop talking about the moon already.

1608
01:02:50,400 --> 01:02:51,700
The sun's already shining on your car.

1609
01:02:51,700 --> 01:02:52,200
Right.

1610
01:02:52,333 --> 01:02:53,100
The moon.

1611
01:02:55,033 --> 01:02:55,800
Right overhead.

1612
01:02:57,633 --> 01:02:59,567
You can see the moon in the daytime every day now.

1613
01:03:00,067 --> 01:03:00,600
It's so annoying.

1614
01:03:00,767 --> 01:03:01,600
Seriously.

1615
01:03:03,267 --> 01:03:03,667
I know.

1616
01:03:04,100 --> 01:03:04,733
You know.

1617
01:03:05,033 --> 01:03:05,633
I know.

1618
01:03:08,567 --> 01:03:09,200
That got a bit heavy.

1619
01:03:09,200 --> 01:03:10,233
We're here to have fun today.

1620
01:03:10,233 --> 01:03:10,767
Yeah.

1621
01:03:12,800 --> 01:03:14,200
Let's go have some fun.

1622
01:03:17,100 --> 01:03:18,200
We've arrived!

1623
01:03:24,100 --> 01:03:25,167
It's cold here

1624
01:03:26,233 --> 01:03:27,733
Seriously, it's pretty cold

1625
01:03:27,733 --> 01:03:29,033
Let's drop off our stuff

1626
01:03:29,233 --> 01:03:30,667
We'll warm up once we get moving

1627
01:03:31,100 --> 01:03:32,467
Good thing I wore long johns

1628
01:03:33,467 --> 01:03:34,433
Alright

1629
01:03:34,433 --> 01:03:36,767
You wore long johns to exercise?

1630
01:03:37,433 --> 01:03:38,167
Are we playing?

1631
01:03:38,167 --> 01:03:38,800
Let's play

1632
01:03:38,800 --> 01:03:39,633
How are we splitting up?

1633
01:03:39,633 --> 01:03:41,400
Let's split into black and white teams

1634
01:03:41,467 --> 01:03:43,267
Us two against you two

1635
01:03:44,433 --> 01:03:45,367
That's a bit unfair

1636
01:03:45,367 --> 01:03:46,000
Just kidding

1637
01:03:46,000 --> 01:03:47,033
Come on, that's too much, teacher

1638
01:03:47,033 --> 01:03:47,767
Black and white teams

1639
01:03:48,300 --> 01:03:48,800
Let's go

1640
01:03:50,167 --> 01:03:51,033
Black

1641
01:03:51,033 --> 01:03:54,267
Black and white pairing

1642
01:03:55,100 --> 01:03:55,467
Alright

1643
01:03:56,533 --> 01:03:57,633
Fate

1644
01:03:57,633 --> 01:03:59,200
The way fate arranged things

1645
01:03:59,300 --> 01:04:00,400
Front or back?

1646
01:04:00,400 --> 01:04:01,100
Me

1647
01:04:01,500 --> 01:04:02,267
I don't really get it

1648
01:04:02,267 --> 01:04:02,800
I'm easy, whatever works

1649
01:04:02,800 --> 01:04:03,300
Me again

1650
01:04:04,300 --> 01:04:05,000
I'm relying on you

1651
01:04:05,000 --> 01:04:06,300
I'm just here to get lucky

1652
01:04:06,300 --> 01:04:07,133
Let's go

1653
01:04:07,800 --> 01:04:11,400
I chose the black and white pairing because I was worried Liang Tian might feel a bit awkward, just in case

1654
01:04:11,400 --> 01:04:13,367
She might feel a little uncomfortable

1655
01:04:13,367 --> 01:04:15,367
Because today

1656
01:04:15,367 --> 01:04:17,100
When I invited her to play badminton

1657
01:04:17,100 --> 01:04:18,200
She probably didn't know yet

1658
01:04:18,200 --> 01:04:19,767
that Yonghao would be joining us

1659
01:04:20,133 --> 01:04:22,133
But in the end, fate had its own plans

1660
01:04:22,133 --> 01:04:24,367
There's nothing we can do about it

1661
01:04:25,700 --> 01:04:26,667
Everyone's really nice

1662
01:04:26,667 --> 01:04:28,167
Xiaxia is great too

1663
01:04:28,167 --> 01:04:30,667
Badminton is a group activity

1664
01:04:30,667 --> 01:04:34,600
And exercise really helps people relax

1665
01:04:34,600 --> 01:04:37,200
I think she could use some exercise too

1666
01:04:37,433 --> 01:04:38,500
I didn't win back the hat game last time

1667
01:04:38,500 --> 01:04:39,467
But today, I'm going to win it all back

1668
01:04:44,367 --> 01:04:45,267
What are you up to?

1669
01:04:45,700 --> 01:04:46,800
I'm pretty agile.

1670
01:04:46,800 --> 01:04:48,133
Yeah, except when it comes to strength,

1671
01:04:48,133 --> 01:04:49,100
I'm actually good at everything else.

1672
01:04:55,167 --> 01:04:57,367
I was a bit surprised to be paired with Luo Junfan.

1673
01:04:58,133 --> 01:04:59,200
It caught me off guard.

1674
01:04:59,200 --> 01:05:01,367
He's actually pretty good at badminton—better than I expected.

1675
01:05:03,167 --> 01:05:03,567
Not bad at all.

1676
01:05:03,567 --> 01:05:07,000
Xia Xia really has an eye for noticing what's great about Luo Junfan.

1677
01:05:07,500 --> 01:05:08,100
Yeah.

1678
01:05:08,700 --> 01:05:10,267
Most of the time, only Xia Xia seems to notice.

1679
01:05:10,400 --> 01:05:12,633
Old Su...

1680
01:05:14,300 --> 01:05:15,267
Oh no.

1681
01:05:15,267 --> 01:05:16,267
With him here today...

1682
01:05:16,267 --> 01:05:17,267
Things are going to get awkward.

1683
01:05:17,467 --> 01:05:19,300
Those two are actually getting along pretty naturally now.

1684
01:05:20,433 --> 01:05:22,600
After we talked things out, it got a lot better. Yeah.

1685
01:05:23,733 --> 01:05:24,500
That was so close!

1686
01:05:24,733 --> 01:05:25,733
It's this light—it's just not good.

1687
01:05:25,733 --> 01:05:26,800
This light is too bright...

1688
01:05:26,800 --> 01:05:28,133
It really gets in your eyes.

1689
01:05:28,133 --> 01:05:29,433
Yeah, this light is no good.

1690
01:05:30,767 --> 01:05:32,167
He's so cute.

1691
01:05:32,167 --> 01:05:32,667
Your turn.

1692
01:05:36,100 --> 01:05:36,533
Come on, Old Su.

1693
01:05:36,533 --> 01:05:37,133
I'll go.

1694
01:05:38,700 --> 01:05:39,233
Okay.

1695
01:05:39,233 --> 01:05:40,067
You go.

1696
01:05:41,167 --> 01:05:42,500
Actually, when I'm paired with Liang Tian,

1697
01:05:42,500 --> 01:05:44,700
I really like how she speaks up.

1698
01:05:44,700 --> 01:05:45,433
She'll say, "I'll get this one,"

1699
01:05:45,433 --> 01:05:46,200
"You take that one,"

1700
01:05:46,200 --> 01:05:47,133
So playing with her

1701
01:05:47,133 --> 01:05:48,200
is actually really easy.

1702
01:05:51,433 --> 01:05:54,667
She does her part really well,

1703
01:05:54,667 --> 01:05:57,233
so I just have to cover the rest.

1704
01:05:57,233 --> 01:05:58,767
Honestly,

1705
01:05:58,767 --> 01:06:02,200
it's the kind of happiness that makes me wish every day could be like this.

1706
01:06:06,367 --> 01:06:08,767
Feels like they're always targeting my side.

1707
01:06:12,000 --> 01:06:12,533
Watch this.

1708
01:06:12,533 --> 01:06:13,500
Now I'm coming at your side.

1709
01:06:14,200 --> 01:06:15,700
Trying to "kill" me, Old Su?

1710
01:06:15,700 --> 01:06:17,067
How dare you try to "kill" me!

1711
01:06:17,267 --> 01:06:18,333
He's so aggressive!

1712
01:06:18,333 --> 01:06:19,300
That's way too much!

1713
01:06:20,000 --> 01:06:21,600
Luo Junfan isn't cutting me any slack.

1714
01:06:23,100 --> 01:06:23,767
It's three to one.

1715
01:06:24,300 --> 01:06:25,000
Much appreciated.

1716
01:06:25,000 --> 01:06:25,500
That's so mean.

1717
01:06:25,500 --> 01:06:26,367
How about you guys take a break?

1718
01:06:26,367 --> 01:06:28,167
How about the two of us play a round?

1719
01:06:28,333 --> 01:06:28,733
Alright, let's do it.

1720
01:06:28,733 --> 01:06:29,367
Let's play, just the two of us.

1721
01:06:29,367 --> 01:06:29,800
Come on.

1722
01:06:30,767 --> 01:06:32,000
I'll come over.

1723
01:06:38,100 --> 01:06:39,267
Alright, the "Business Ball" game is underway.

1724
01:06:39,400 --> 01:06:41,433
Business ball!

1725
01:06:42,600 --> 01:06:43,800
And now we see Liang Tian.

1726
01:06:43,800 --> 01:06:45,133
She serves from the side.

1727
01:06:45,300 --> 01:06:46,167
That was a gentle touch.

1728
01:06:46,500 --> 01:06:47,433
Nice, scooping it up from below.

1729
01:06:47,433 --> 01:06:48,500
She kept it low.

1730
01:06:48,500 --> 01:06:50,433
That ball almost grazed the edge.

1731
01:06:50,433 --> 01:06:52,333
You can tell our player Xia Xia

1732
01:06:52,767 --> 01:06:53,667
only knows how to scoop from underneath.

1733
01:06:55,067 --> 01:06:56,100
Is her pro side coming out?

1734
01:06:56,633 --> 01:06:57,433
Stir-frying!

1735
01:06:57,767 --> 01:06:59,600
You can tell right away she's got what it takes to be a chef.

1736
01:06:59,600 --> 01:07:00,267
Definitely.

1737
01:07:00,467 --> 01:07:01,333
Thanks, everyone.

1738
01:07:04,667 --> 01:07:06,000
Twelve to ten

1739
01:07:06,000 --> 01:07:06,600
A narrow loss

1740
01:07:06,600 --> 01:07:08,467
A close defeat

1741
01:07:08,700 --> 01:07:10,333
We mainly lost because of your slouchy socks.

1742
01:07:10,633 --> 01:07:11,733
Take off your slouchy socks.

1743
01:07:13,700 --> 01:07:14,667
Seriously, take off your slouchy socks.

1744
01:07:15,433 --> 01:07:16,200
The whole time

1745
01:07:16,200 --> 01:07:18,700
I thought the atmosphere was really, really good.

1746
01:07:18,700 --> 01:07:20,500
Let me go change into my slouchy socks first.

1747
01:07:22,067 --> 01:07:22,567
What's up?

1748
01:07:22,567 --> 01:07:23,067
What?

1749
01:07:23,067 --> 01:07:23,233
No.

1750
01:07:23,233 --> 01:07:25,333
There's nothing wrong with me changing my slouchy socks.

1751
01:07:26,367 --> 01:07:27,567
If you don't keep them in line, they'll run wild.

1752
01:07:27,800 --> 01:07:28,667
Those two are actually kind of...

1753
01:07:29,433 --> 01:07:30,300
Even a bit...

1754
01:07:30,300 --> 01:07:30,667
Inexplicable.

1755
01:07:30,667 --> 01:07:31,433
Yeah.

1756
01:07:31,433 --> 01:07:32,667
They really made me feel so awkward, seriously.

1757
01:07:32,667 --> 01:07:34,100
Looks like they're back at it again.

1758
01:07:34,467 --> 01:07:35,233
Seriously.

1759
01:07:35,233 --> 01:07:37,167
Luo did it all on his own—

1760
01:07:37,167 --> 01:07:39,167
He really got everyone hyped up.

1761
01:07:40,000 --> 01:07:41,533
So even now, I feel

1762
01:07:41,533 --> 01:07:42,467
like Xia Xia and I

1763
01:07:42,467 --> 01:07:46,200
are back to square one—as just friends.

1764
01:07:46,200 --> 01:07:47,067
What's your score?

1765
01:07:47,067 --> 01:07:48,000
Four to three.

1766
01:07:50,467 --> 01:07:51,700
And mine?

1767
01:07:51,700 --> 01:07:53,567
No need to thank me.

1768
01:07:54,500 --> 01:07:57,033
You didn't even let me answer before you hit!

1769
01:07:57,033 --> 01:07:57,700
What's your score?

1770
01:08:07,200 --> 01:08:07,767
No need to thank me.

1771
01:08:07,767 --> 01:08:09,600
No need to kneel.

1772
01:08:09,733 --> 01:08:11,467
Seriously, you're welcome.

1773
01:08:15,033 --> 01:08:15,767
I feel like going out with everyone

1774
01:08:15,767 --> 01:08:17,300
really helps me relax and adjust my mood

1775
01:08:17,300 --> 01:08:19,100
especially today, since we exercised

1776
01:08:23,000 --> 01:08:23,733
Sure

1777
01:08:24,200 --> 01:08:25,633
I'm just really happy

1778
01:08:25,767 --> 01:08:28,700
Suddenly, I feel much better

1779
01:08:30,500 --> 01:08:31,467
The score is four to eight

1780
01:08:37,000 --> 01:08:38,700
You still want to play business games with me, huh?

1781
01:08:42,300 --> 01:08:43,800
Hey, what's up, kid?

1782
01:08:43,800 --> 01:08:45,800
Did someone's humor get to you? Sent you flying?

1783
01:08:46,333 --> 01:08:48,233
Yeah, it knocked me for a loop.

1784
01:08:48,633 --> 01:08:49,733
No, let me give you all some advice.

1785
01:08:50,100 --> 01:08:52,000
Some guys will make you coffee today,

1786
01:08:52,000 --> 01:08:53,500
but who knows, maybe poison it tomorrow.

1787
01:08:56,033 --> 01:08:58,033
The sun is really bright today.

1788
01:08:59,700 --> 01:09:01,633
I feel like I haven't been out in days.

1789
01:09:01,633 --> 01:09:03,100
It feels so nice.

1790
01:09:03,433 --> 01:09:04,367
Yeah.

1791
01:09:04,500 --> 01:09:07,500
No one's in the house today, right?

1792
01:09:07,767 --> 01:09:09,633
So Yan Yan and I decided to take a walk in the park

1793
01:09:09,633 --> 01:09:10,433
and

1794
01:09:10,433 --> 01:09:12,400
snap some photos.

1795
01:09:14,733 --> 01:09:17,167
This bike looks pretty fun too.

1796
01:09:17,167 --> 01:09:18,100
Can we ride it?

1797
01:09:18,100 --> 01:09:19,200
Yeah, you can.

1798
01:09:19,200 --> 01:09:20,233
Come on.

1799
01:09:21,533 --> 01:09:23,333
Let's give this one a try.

1800
01:09:23,333 --> 01:09:24,067
Come on.

1801
01:09:25,067 --> 01:09:26,000
Is it dirty?

1802
01:09:26,667 --> 01:09:28,067
This part's a bit dirty, right?

1803
01:09:28,467 --> 01:09:29,367
But it seems okay.

1804
01:09:29,367 --> 01:09:30,333
Wipe it off.

1805
01:09:31,167 --> 01:09:32,433
You still have some tissues, right?

1806
01:09:34,767 --> 01:09:36,333
You're so thoughtful.

1807
01:09:36,800 --> 01:09:37,733
Head that way.

1808
01:09:37,733 --> 01:09:39,333
It's really pretty over there.

1809
01:09:39,600 --> 01:09:40,667
I want to take a picture.

1810
01:09:41,333 --> 01:09:42,200
Let me take one for you.

1811
01:09:42,200 --> 01:09:43,367
Yeah, sure.

1812
01:09:46,300 --> 01:09:46,733
How does it look?

1813
01:09:46,733 --> 01:09:47,500
Yeah, it looks good.

1814
01:09:49,667 --> 01:09:50,367
Isn't that too low?

1815
01:09:50,367 --> 01:09:52,067
I like it a bit higher.

1816
01:09:53,567 --> 01:09:54,633
Now it's too high.

1817
01:09:55,533 --> 01:09:56,233
The smart system.

1818
01:09:56,233 --> 01:09:57,767
The smart system is busy.

1819
01:09:57,767 --> 01:10:00,167
Come on, Zhang, sign up for a class already.

1820
01:10:00,167 --> 01:10:01,400
Just hold it like you usually do.

1821
01:10:01,400 --> 01:10:02,567
Just hold it like this.

1822
01:10:04,000 --> 01:10:04,400
Just like that.

1823
01:10:04,400 --> 01:10:06,433
I want a full-body shot.

1824
01:10:06,433 --> 01:10:07,700
I don't want a full-body shot.

1825
01:10:08,500 --> 01:10:10,333
A full-body shot might make you look shorter.

1826
01:10:12,667 --> 01:10:13,600
You're so good at this.

1827
01:10:16,367 --> 01:10:17,567
Set it to 2.4x.

1828
01:10:18,067 --> 01:10:19,767
Try 2x.

1829
01:10:25,667 --> 01:10:27,167
Not bad.

1830
01:10:27,167 --> 01:10:27,733
Yeah.

1831
01:10:28,267 --> 01:10:29,167
Looks so good!

1832
01:10:29,167 --> 01:10:30,067
Right?

1833
01:10:31,367 --> 01:10:32,533
So pretty.

1834
01:10:33,033 --> 01:10:34,500
Let me try from this side and come back.

1835
01:10:35,600 --> 01:10:36,533
Okay.

1836
01:10:38,700 --> 01:10:40,800
That's how you pose for photos.

1837
01:10:43,400 --> 01:10:44,767
This one looks good too.

1838
01:10:45,300 --> 01:10:45,667
It's really not cold when you're taking photos.

1839
01:10:45,667 --> 01:10:48,467
Seriously, you don't feel the cold at all when taking pictures.

1840
01:10:49,033 --> 01:10:51,433
The animals least afraid of the cold in the world:

1841
01:10:51,433 --> 01:10:52,800
penguins, polar bears,

1842
01:10:52,800 --> 01:10:54,567
and women taking photos.

1843
01:10:55,733 --> 01:10:56,367
Exactly!

1844
01:10:58,633 --> 01:10:59,533
What do you think?

1845
01:11:00,333 --> 01:11:01,533
Here, let me take one for you.

1846
01:11:01,533 --> 01:11:02,500
I'm not good at it.

1847
01:11:03,167 --> 01:11:04,133
Now I don't even dare to take photos.

1848
01:11:04,133 --> 01:11:05,167
Are you done?

1849
01:11:05,167 --> 01:11:06,300
This one's nice.

1850
01:11:06,733 --> 01:11:08,300
You gotta get your stuff ready.

1851
01:11:10,333 --> 01:11:11,633
Zhang, you've really got the vibe down.

1852
01:11:13,000 --> 01:11:14,200
Nice.

1853
01:11:17,500 --> 01:11:18,700
Let's skip this pose.

1854
01:11:22,533 --> 01:11:24,433
This isn't a pose you'd pick.

1855
01:11:25,467 --> 01:11:28,000
No, I suddenly got nervous when you started taking my picture.

1856
01:11:28,000 --> 01:11:28,700
Nervous?

1857
01:11:28,700 --> 01:11:29,500
Yeah.

1858
01:11:30,167 --> 01:11:32,600
Try moving around a bit.

1859
01:11:33,067 --> 01:11:33,667
Right.

1860
01:11:33,667 --> 01:11:34,567
Same here.

1861
01:11:36,800 --> 01:11:38,233
Now Zhang's confident.

1862
01:11:39,567 --> 01:11:42,033
I think you should loosen up the pose a bit.

1863
01:11:42,033 --> 01:11:43,100
Just relax a bit.

1864
01:11:43,500 --> 01:11:44,733
That's it, looks great.

1865
01:11:45,333 --> 01:11:46,600
Very natural.

1866
01:11:48,067 --> 01:11:48,300
That works.

1867
01:11:48,300 --> 01:11:49,400
That looks really good.

1868
01:11:49,400 --> 01:11:49,700
Looks great.

1869
01:11:50,700 --> 01:11:51,633
Double speed.

1870
01:11:53,667 --> 01:11:56,500
I've already memorized the double speed.

1871
01:11:56,733 --> 01:11:59,400
All of Zhang's moments today are in double time.

1872
01:11:59,400 --> 01:12:00,800
When you turned a bit to the side just now—

1873
01:12:00,800 --> 01:12:02,167
—that looked great.

1874
01:12:06,133 --> 01:12:08,000
We got some good photos today.

1875
01:12:08,633 --> 01:12:09,200
Alright, let's go.

1876
01:12:09,200 --> 01:12:10,567
Let's go ride bikes.

1877
01:12:11,500 --> 01:12:12,600
Careful.

1878
01:12:13,633 --> 01:12:15,133
Here I go!

1879
01:12:15,133 --> 01:12:16,333
Let's go for it!

1880
01:12:17,267 --> 01:12:18,433
Man, it's cold.

1881
01:12:24,233 --> 01:12:26,133
How about I make us some Western food today?

1882
01:12:26,133 --> 01:12:28,500
Today, I’ll just make dinner for the two of us.

1883
01:12:29,433 --> 01:12:31,433
Go light on the garlic and onions.

1884
01:12:31,433 --> 01:12:32,300
You’re okay with that, right?

1885
01:12:32,300 --> 01:12:32,700
Yeah.

1886
01:12:32,700 --> 01:12:34,267
That’s pretty direct.

1887
01:12:34,267 --> 01:12:35,300
But it’s nice.

1888
01:12:35,300 --> 01:12:35,667
Yeah.

1889
01:12:35,667 --> 01:12:37,300
Just like that time we were up on the mountain.

1890
01:12:37,300 --> 01:12:38,600
I think it was after we got Lao Su’s letter.

1891
01:12:38,600 --> 01:12:42,000
He said you two have a lot in common.

1892
01:12:42,000 --> 01:12:43,667
He was talking about Liang Tian, wasn’t he?

1893
01:12:46,333 --> 01:12:47,433
I was so surprised.

1894
01:12:47,433 --> 01:12:49,633
It was like discovering a whole new world.

1895
01:12:51,100 --> 01:12:52,367
That’s so cute.

1896
01:12:52,367 --> 01:12:54,200
Now that’s what I call a beautiful misunderstanding.

1897
01:12:54,200 --> 01:12:55,400
It was such a nice surprise.

1898
01:12:55,400 --> 01:12:57,800
I don’t have to overthink things anymore.

1899
01:12:57,800 --> 01:12:59,633
And I don’t have to worry about gains and losses anymore.

1900
01:12:59,633 --> 01:13:02,667
This is so much fun.

1901
01:13:06,300 --> 01:13:07,167
Hello.

1902
01:13:07,167 --> 01:13:08,533
My old crush.

1903
01:13:12,367 --> 01:13:14,467
I was really treading carefully.

1904
01:13:14,467 --> 01:13:16,300
Honestly, it was actually pretty stifling.

1905
01:13:16,300 --> 01:13:18,300
I tried to mentally prepare myself by thinking,

1906
01:13:18,300 --> 01:13:20,400
"this is just something I have to go through."

1907
01:13:20,767 --> 01:13:21,700
Over the past couple of days,

1908
01:13:21,700 --> 01:13:24,033
I just happened to see that she wasn't feeling too good.

1909
01:13:24,433 --> 01:13:26,033
And I think

1910
01:13:26,033 --> 01:13:28,100
I'm one of the people she's a bit closer to.

1911
01:13:28,100 --> 01:13:31,133
So I thought I'd use this song to express how I feel.

1912
01:13:31,133 --> 01:13:33,433
She really has made her way into my heart.

1913
01:13:33,433 --> 01:13:36,633
You really caught me by surprise.

1914
01:13:36,633 --> 01:13:37,600
What the heck?

1915
01:13:39,800 --> 01:13:41,533
During these two days and one night, everyone gets a chance.

1916
01:13:41,533 --> 01:13:42,633
But the question is, who do you go with,

1917
01:13:42,633 --> 01:13:43,700
and who does the inviting?

1918
01:13:51,400 --> 01:13:52,400
Who is it?

1919
01:14:00,433 --> 01:14:02,300
Any funny stories after the show aired?

1920
01:14:02,300 --> 01:14:03,500
Season 4 of "Half-Grown Lovers"—what's up with that?

1921
01:14:03,500 --> 01:14:04,667
Left hand: top tier.

1922
01:14:04,667 --> 01:14:05,533
Right hand...

1923
01:14:06,533 --> 01:14:07,533
That's insane!

1924
01:14:09,200 --> 01:14:11,133
What's up with that face?

1925
01:14:11,133 --> 01:14:13,100
Why did I even say that?

1926
01:14:13,100 --> 01:14:15,233
Save me, Teacher Hou!

1927
01:14:15,233 --> 01:14:17,033
I was so moved when I saw Xiao Hou's letters.

1928
01:14:17,033 --> 01:14:18,067
I was really touched.

1929
01:14:18,067 --> 01:14:19,200
Xiao Hou is so sweet.

1930
01:14:20,500 --> 01:14:21,767
You two are already this close?

1931
01:14:22,300 --> 01:14:23,467
From my god's-eye view...

1932
01:14:23,800 --> 01:14:27,067
This is so sweet, bro, I'm a little jealous.

1933
01:14:27,067 --> 01:14:29,067
This is all for you, bro.

1934
01:14:29,067 --> 01:14:30,333
I think I still need to work on my facial expressions.

1935
01:14:30,333 --> 01:14:32,400
Not good enough yet.

1936
01:14:34,100 --> 01:14:37,400
I can move both my eyebrows like this.

1937
01:14:38,467 --> 01:14:39,767
Just like, you know, moving that thing.

1938
01:14:46,033 --> 01:14:48,433
You're not afraid of long-distance relationships at all.

1939
01:14:48,433 --> 01:14:49,300
I'm a little afraid.

1940
01:14:49,300 --> 01:14:51,700
But it seems like the more I'm afraid of something, the more likely it is to happen.

1941
01:14:51,700 --> 01:14:52,600
I've been in four relationships, and all of them were long-distance.

1942
01:14:52,600 --> 01:14:54,200
I've been in four relationships, and all of them were long-distance.

1943
01:14:54,767 --> 01:14:55,800
But if you're living alone now,

1944
01:14:55,800 --> 01:14:56,767
maybe you could get a kitten or something.

1945
01:14:57,067 --> 01:14:58,333
But I really don't think it's a good idea for just one person

1946
01:14:58,333 --> 01:14:59,167
to have a pet.

1947
01:14:59,167 --> 01:15:00,267
I mean, what if something happens to you?

1948
01:15:00,267 --> 01:15:02,200
You need someone on standby at home.

1949
01:15:02,433 --> 01:15:04,033
The backup is ready to jump in!
